---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  path="/en/terms"
  altPath="/terms"
  title="Terms of Service · Law Portal"
  description="The terms governing your use of the Law Portal platform, for both clients and lawyers."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-ink">Terms of Service</h1>

    <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-warning bg-warning-tint p-4 text-sm text-ink">
      <strong>Note:</strong> this is a first-draft template for this stage of the product, not final legal text. It
      must be reviewed by licensed counsel before launch and adoption as a binding terms of use contract.
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-soft">
      <p>Last updated: <span class="font-mono">2026-08-03</span></p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">1. Nature of the service</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Law Portal is an intermediary platform connecting clients seeking legal services with lawyers licensed by
          the Saudi Ministry of Justice. The platform itself does not provide legal advice or opinion, and is not a
          substitute for the direct professional relationship between a client and the lawyer delivering the
          service.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">2. Accounts and verification</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Users must provide accurate information at registration. Every lawyer's registration is subject to an
          administrative review of their Ministry of Justice licence before their profile appears in the directory
          or they may receive any request. The platform reserves the right to reject or suspend any account that
          submits inaccurate licence information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">3. Payment and commission</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          A client's funds are held in escrow until the service is complete or a price offer is accepted, then
          released to the lawyer net of the platform's agreed commission. A tax invoice is issued for every
          completed payment under Saudi VAT regulation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">4. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If a lawyer declines a paid request, the full amount is automatically refunded to the client. Cancellations
          after service delivery has begun are assessed on a case-by-case basis.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">5. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The platform is responsible for the reliable operation of its technical service (payment, messaging,
          scheduling), and is not responsible for the quality or outcome of the legal consultation or service
          delivered by a lawyer, which remains that lawyer's direct professional responsibility to the client.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">6. Governing law</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, and its courts have exclusive
          jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">7. Account deletion</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Any user may request account deletion at any time from their account settings, subject to retaining
          financial records for the period required by law.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
